ubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135327750,imgsize-261986.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[UT students wanted to condemn comments targeting Indian-origin students but university thought it was not just Bo French]]></title><description><![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/ut-students-wanted-to-condemn-comments-targeting-indian-origin-students-but-university-thought-it-was-not-just-bo-french/articleshow/135326760.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/ut-students-wanted-to-condemn-comments-targeting-indian-origin-students-but-university-thought-it-was-not-just-bo-french/articleshow/135326760.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-30T00:03:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135327047,imgsize-206160.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2022, conservators X-raying a Van Gogh painting in Edinburgh found a hidden self-portrait of the artist on the back of the canvas, concealed for more than a century under layers of glue and cardboard]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135308668.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A self-portrait of Vincent van Gogh was discovered concealed behind another painting after many years. The hidden portrait was found during routine examinations ahead of an exhibition. This discovery highlights Van Gogh's habit of reusing canvases due to financial difficulties throughout his life. Conservators are now working to reveal the portrait without damaging the original painting. Visitors to the exhibition were able to view the hidden portrait's X-ray image.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-2022-conservators-x-raying-a-van-gogh-painting-in-edinburgh-found-a-hidden-self-portrait-of-the-artist-on-the-back-of-the-canvas-concealed-for-more-than-a-century-under-layers-of-glue-and-cardboard/articleshow/135308668.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-2022-conservators-x-raying-a-van-gogh-painting-in-edinburgh-found-a-hidden-self-portrait-of-the-artist-on-the-back-of-the-canvas-concealed-for-more-than-a-century-under-layers-of-glue-and-cardboard/articleshow/135308668.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-29T22:02:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135314787,imgsize-1910252.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Michigan family builds pirate hip Halloween display with live actors on October 31]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135297967.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-father-and-his-family-have-added-a-pirate-ship-to-their-front-yard-halloween-world-complete-with-blue-lighting-and-skeleton-sailors-with-live-actors-set-to-take-over-on-october-31/articleshow/135297967.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-father-and-his-family-have-added-a-pirate-ship-to-their-front-yard-halloween-world-complete-with-blue-lighting-and-skeleton-sailors-with-live-actors-set-to-take-over-on-october-31/articleshow/135297967.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-30T04:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135298089,imgsize-918264.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Texas man Christophe Waggoner began October's Child in 2017; has gifted 8,000 Halloween costumes to families and plans to give away 4,000 in 2026]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135296088.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Christophe Waggoner established a charity called October's Child to provide Halloween costumes for children. He began the initiative after recalling his own childhood experiences with costumes. Over the years, the charity has grown significantly, distributing nearly 8,000 costumes to families in need. In the upcoming event, he plans to give away over 4,000 costumes for various age groups. Waggoner's efforts illustrate the positive impact of community support on childhood celebrations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/growing-up-without-being-able-to-afford-halloween-costumes-texas-man-christophe-waggoner-began-octobers-child-in-2017-he-has-gifted-8000-costumes-to-families-and-plans-to-give-away-4000-in-2026/articleshow/135296088.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/growing-up-without-being-able-to-afford-halloween-costumes-texas-man-christophe-waggoner-began-octobers-child-in-2017-he-has-gifted-8000-costumes-to-families-and-plans-to-give-away-4000-in-2026/articleshow/135296088.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-30T02:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135296824,imgsize-1612533.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Inside Bieber Couple's Condo: Justin and Hailey add $12m West Village home; waterfront NYC base]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135288692.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Justin and Hailey Bieber have acquired a $12 million condominium in Manhattan's West Village. This residence features expansive river views and distinct architectural design. The apartment includes four bedrooms and significant amenities for privacy and convenience. The property reflects a modernist style and includes shared amenities like a swimming pool. This purchase adds to the couple's diverse real estate portfolio that spans multiple locations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/justin-and-hailey-biebers-manhattan-condo-reportedly-cost-12-million-the-four-bedroom-residence-features-a-120-foot-wall-of-windows-overlooking-the-hudson-river/articleshow/135288692.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/justin-and-hailey-biebers-manhattan-condo-reportedly-cost-12-million-the-four-bedroom-residence-features-a-120-foot-wall-of-windows-overlooking-the-hudson-river/articleshow/135288692.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-30T01:56:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Khushi</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135288731,imgsize-1792336.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[After 20-Year Search, California Community Buys Cupertino Property for $16.5 Million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135270044.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[After an extensive search, the West Valley Muslim Association has successfully acquired a property in Cupertino for $16.5 million. This new facility will serve as a permanent home for the community, offering a venue for daily prayers, educational activities, and community gatherings. Supported by a dedicated fundraising campaign, this purchase reflects the growing needs of the local Muslim population, establishing a vital center for faith and fellowship.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-california-community-searched-nearly-20-years-for-a-permanent-place-to-gather-and-worship-after-raising-funds-and-beating-competing-offers-it-completed-a-16-5-million-cupertino-property-purchase-on-october-22/articleshow/135270044.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-california-community-searched-nearly-20-years-for-a-permanent-place-to-gather-and-worship-after-raising-funds-and-beating-competing-offers-it-completed-a-16-5-million-cupertino-property-purchase-on-october-22/articleshow/135270044.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-30T01:51:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135270220,imgsize-142020.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[3,700-year-old man buried with stone in his mouth beneath a hearth may have been part of magical ritual]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135297234.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Approximately 3,700 years ago, a man in southeastern Spain underwent a burial unlike any other. Researchers suggest that this ritual may have been intended to symbolically overcome a threat rather than inflict punishment. The discovery of his body underneath a hearth, with a stone in his mouth, implies an effort to silence him.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/he-was-buried-beneath-a-hearth-with-a-large-stone-pressed-against-his-mouth-and-face-just-one-cm-below-the-floor-people-walked-on-researchers-now-suggest-the-3700-year-old-burial-was-part-of-a-magical-ritual-not-a-punishment/articleshow/135297234.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/he-was-buried-beneath-a-hearth-with-a-large-stone-pressed-against-his-mouth-and-face-just-one-cm-below-the-floor-people-walked-on-researchers-now-suggest-the-3700-year-old-burial-was-part-of-a-magical-ritual-not-a-punishment/articleshow/135297234.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-30T00:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135297442,imgsize-1733972.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[How UKHarvest turned food waste into 10 million meals]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135239446.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 2017, Yvonne Thomson founded UKHarvest to address food waste and assist individuals facing food insecurity. Initially starting with one van, the charity has impressively salvaged 10 million meals throughout its journey. Its initiatives, including Community Food Hubs and Grub Clubs, offer not only affordable food but also valuable education. Collecting about 10 tonnes of excess food weekly, UKHarvest enjoys the patronage of Queen Camilla, amplifying its community impact.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-2017-a-british-food-rescue-organisation-started-with-one-person-and-a-van-collecting-surplus-food-nine-years-later-ukharvest-has-rescued-10-million-meals-and-now-collects-10-tonnes-of-surplus-food-every-week/articleshow/135239446.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-2017-a-british-food-rescue-organisation-started-with-one-person-and-a-van-collecting-surplus-food-nine-years-later-ukharvest-has-rescued-10-million-meals-and-now-collects-10-tonnes-of-surplus-food-every-week/articleshow/135239446.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-30T00:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135239618,imgsize-167278.cms"/></item></channel></rss>